      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T19:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "... yup, and I think I found it. Most of the code-gen inside the SkSL -\u003e skvm logic does boil things down before ever calling functions. The first diff (r12) is from a comparison against 100.5, which was the big clue - that\u0027s for the new pixel tracing logic. Sure enough, trace-mask is created via an expression that looks like:\n\n  fTraceMask \u003d (device.x \u003d\u003d traceCoord.x) \u0026 (device.y \u003d\u003d traceCoord.y);\n  \nSo the evaluation of the two inputs to operator\u0026 are going to be eval\u0027d in a different order, resulting in differently numbered temporaries. Easy fix.",
      "parentUuid": "fdcee6f8_7061d450",
      "range": {
